# Nexus-Hub Project Rules

Canonical source: `AGENTS.md` at repo root. Cursor reads this `.mdc` file plus `AGENTS.md` automatically; the essentials are summarized here for quick reference.

## Golden rule: installer-aware changes

Nexus-Hub is a **template repository**. Nothing is "live" until a user runs `scripts/installer.sh` (macOS/Linux) or `scripts/installer.ps1` (Windows). Every change must be shaped so that after the next installer run, it reaches every supported platform (Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini, OpenCode, Copilot) on Windows, macOS, and Linux, without any manual step.

## Quick reference

1. **New file under `scripts/<name>.{py,js}`**: MUST be registered in BOTH `scripts/installer.sh` (near line 1395, next to `generate_report.py`) AND `scripts/installer.ps1` (near line 1656). The installer copies scripts by explicit name, never by folder. Pattern: see the existing `generate_report.py` copy block.

2. **New skill** (`catalog/skills/<cat>/<name>/SKILL.md`): update three registry files — `data/SKILL_INDEX.md`, `data/skills.json`, `data/marketplace.json`. The skill folder is auto-copied. A **new category** must also be listed in `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` `skills` (`./catalog/skills/<cat>`).

3. **New command** (`catalog/commands/<name>.md`): no registry update; folder auto-copied. If the command needs a style-guide reference, place it at `catalog/style-guides/<name>.md` (NOT in `catalog/commands/`, otherwise it surfaces as a slash command). Command-derived skills emit `disable-model-invocation: true` from `_synthesize_skill` (shared Python; no installer copy step). Do not invent a per-platform lever.

4. **New hook** (`catalog/hooks/<name>.{sh,py}`): register in `catalog/hooks/settings.json`; add tests under `catalog/hooks/tests/`.

5. **Platform instruction templates** (`templates/ai-instructions/base-*.md`): edit all five (claude/codex/cursor/gemini/opencode) in lockstep — changes must be platform-agnostic.

6. **Document template** (`templates/documentation/<name>.{docx,pptx,xlsx,...}`): folder auto-copied; no installer change.

7. **Never edit `data/*.json` manually** except the three registry files in rule 2.

8. **Never commit secrets.** Respected by the `secret-scan.sh` hook.

9. **Validate** after any change: `make validate`, `make lint`, `make test` (for new hooks). Dry-run the installer when you touch installer code.

10. **Document** user-visible changes under `## [Unreleased]` in `CHANGELOG.md`.

## MCP Registry Policy

Nexus-Hub's MCP registry (`catalog/mcp-configs/mcp-servers.json`) is governed by a strict decision tree. When proposing a new entry, walk it in order and stop at the first bucket that fits:

1. **Local-only** (internal Nexus-Hub servers or zero-outbound Anthropic-official servers) - always allowed.
2. **LLM-native skill** (capability achievable by instructing the agent directly) - ship a skill, not an MCP.
3. **Reverse-engineer into a local internal MCP** - if the external project's logic can run locally, build the internal equivalent under `extensions/`. Strip external-source attribution; use generic descriptive names.
4. **Trusted vendor wrapper (your-own-account)** - acceptable only when the vendor is the intrinsic data destination, reverse-engineering isn't viable, AND the feature is extremely worth it. Justify all three in the `_comment`.
5. **Otherwise** - drop.

Hard no: search-as-service, embeddings-as-service, scraping-as-service, generation-as-service. Full policy + 5-question audit in `AGENTS.md`. Matrix at `docs/policy/mcp-reverse-engineering-matrix.md`.

## Platform coverage caveat

The installer currently deploys per-file skill/command/agent trees only to Claude Code, Gemini, and Codex. Cursor, OpenCode, and Copilot receive behavioral guardrails only. New slash commands are not reachable as `/...` on those three platforms - note this in the CHANGELOG.

These rules apply only to work inside this repo.
